{
  "$schema": "../../schemas/apps.schema.json",
  "comment": [
    "This is the app catalog for the whole tenant, not just the child tier. Required security and",
    "Microsoft 365 clients install automatically for the tier they target; other approved apps remain",
    "available in Company Portal but cannot be installed until declared here.",
    "Android entries are added through the Managed Google Play connector configured in the tenant.",
    "Windows entries use source=existing: Microsoft Store (new)/winget-backed apps cannot be created",
    "over Graph the way Managed Google Play and iOS Store apps can, so the app must be added once in",
    "the Intune admin center (Apps > Windows > Add > Microsoft Store app (new), searching the exact",
    "displayName below) before this repo can manage its assignment. A 'Prerequisite' action reports",
    "cleanly in plan mode, but blocks the reviewed-plan deployment gate entirely (it counts the same",
    "as Skip) - so no Windows entry should be added to this catalog until its Intune bootstrap step",
    "is done. Moonlight/Windows App/Xbox for Windows are intentionally deferred for this reason; see",
    "the sg-nuclear-family decision log for the bootstrap steps to add them in a follow-up.",
    "2026-08-19: Microsoft merged the consumer Copilot app and the Microsoft 365 Copilot (work or school)",
    "app into a single unified 'Microsoft Copilot' app (rollout started August 2026). The rebrand updates",
    "the existing app entries in place - Google Play/App Store confirm the packageId/bundleId are",
    "unchanged - so renamed 'android-m365-copilot'/'ios-m365-copilot' to 'android-copilot'/'ios-copilot'",
    "and updated displayName to 'Microsoft Copilot' on both to match the live app identity. This also",
    "fixes deploys blocking on fail-closed one-time adoption for the Android entry, whose live tenant",
    "object's displayName had already been renamed by the Play Store update, no longer matching the old",
    "configured displayName.",
    "2026-08-19: left the iOS entry's appStoreUrl on the old 'microsoft-365-copilot' slug (it 301-redirects",
    "to the new 'microsoft-copilot' slug, same numeric app id, so it still works) - Graph rejects PATCH",
    "requests that change an existing iosStoreApp's appStoreUrl ('AppStoreUrl cannot be patched'), so",
    "updating the slug in config breaks deploy for an object that already exists in the tenant. displayName",
    "is still updated to 'Microsoft Copilot' since that field is patchable.",
    "2026-08-19: ios-onedrive's appStoreUrl has a trailing '?uo=4' query param, matching what the Intune",
    "portal's app picker attached when the object was manually re-created after an accidental deletion.",
    "Update never PATCHes appStoreUrl for an iosStoreApp (see the appStoreUrl note above), so this would",
    "otherwise show as permanent, never-resolving drift in every future plan; matching the live value",
    "here instead is harmless since Deploy already treats that field as immutable post-creation."
  ],
